Subject: [PATCH 93/98] Journal opens again: incursion encounter rewards

The journal's Incursions tab lists the encounters with the most LP and ISK
each pays, and asks rewardMgr.GetRewardData for them when the window
opens if that list was ever expanded. The server didn't have it, so the
client got None and the journal wouldn't open at all.

GetRewardData now returns the payout table for scout, vanguard, assault,
headquarters and mothership sites, worked out the same way site payouts
are: a full fleet's pay up to the site's fleet size (scaled by FleetScale),
split between the pilots above that, and 10/7 of it in low and null-sec.
With DelayedLP the LP is listed as a delayed reward. An unknown rewardID
gets empty tables. rewardTypeLP is 1 (from the client's traceback); ISK as
2 and the security criteria as 1 and 2 are guesses, since no client source
I could find has the constants.
